<Project>

  <!-- Inherit everything from the repo root, then relax what only makes sense for shipped APIs. -->
  <Import Project="$([MSBuild]::GetPathOfFileAbove('Directory.Build.props', '$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)../'))" />

  <!--
    Two rules are off for test projects only. Both are public-API rules being applied to code that
    is not a public API.

    CA1707 — "remove the underscores from member name".
      The engine-conventions skill requires test names to read as sentences:
      Undo_continues_after_one_step_fails. That is the single most useful thing about the suite
      when something breaks, and it is worth more than matching a naming rule aimed at libraries
      other people consume.

    CA1816 — "call GC.SuppressFinalize in Dispose".
      xUnit fixtures implement IDisposable to delete a temp folder. None of them has a finalizer
      and none is meant to be derived from, so the ceremony would add noise without adding safety.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CA1707;CA1816</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
